target: skills/review/review-loop/runlog.py
verify: bash skills/review/review-loop/runlog.test.sh
expect: FAIL  undocumented flags (or a broken check): plan:--session-kind
why:    the first version of this guard checked `cycle` alone, which is one of ten subcommands, and plan, carried and check each had a live undocumented flag at that moment. The synopsis is printed verbatim by --help, so a reader sees a complete-looking flag list with one missing. Checking a single subcommand is fixing the instance that was noticed rather than the class, which is what produced four separate passes for one flag.
--- old
                    [--run-id <id>] [--session-kind <k>]
--- new
                    [--run-id <id>]
